statement:
You are given two positive integers `x` and `y`. Each operation changes `x` in one of four ways:

- if `x` is divisible by 11, replace it with `x / 11`;
- if `x` is divisible by 5, replace it with `x / 5`;
- subtract 1 from `x`;
- add 1 to `x`.

Return the fewest operations needed to turn `x` into `y`.

validator:
function validate([x, y]) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(x) || x < 1 || x > 10000) return 'x is an integer from 1 to 10^4.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(y) || y < 1 || y > 10000) return 'y is an integer from 1 to 10^4.';
  return null;
}

